<title>EGYPT: Tora Cement ups 95/96 profits 27 pct.</title>
<headline>Tora Cement ups 95/96 profits 27 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian Portland Tora Cement said on Sunday it raised net distributable profits for the 1995/96 financial year by more than 27 percent to 212.41 million pounds from 167.12 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>The financial year ends on June 30.</p>
<p>The firm, one of Egypt's leading cement manufacturers, also said net sales were higher at 499.54 million compared to 457.41 million in 1994/95.</p>
<p>Tora Cement's shares are among the most actively traded on the Egyptian stock exchange. On Sunday, the stock ended unchanged at 60.00 pounds from Thursday's close.</p>
<p>Here are details of the firm's balance sheet and profit and loss account (figures in millions of pounds):</p>
<p>					1995/96	  1994/95</p>
<p>    FIXED ASSETS		  373.60	   403.29</p>
<p>    CURRENT LIABILITIES	 279.65	   261.66</p>
<p>    OPERATING PROFITS	   169.20	   147.24</p>
<p>    GROSS PROFITS		 137.90	   150.58</p>
<p>    PRE-TAX PROFITS	     169.77	   155.52</p>
<p>$1 = 3.4 Egyptian pounds</p>
<p>-- Miral Fahmy + 202 578 3290/91</p>
